<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahmud Shah II of Johor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1675">1675</a>–<a href="/years/1699">1699</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahmud Shah II was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a> from 1685 to 1699 and the last ruler descended from the sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a>. He came to the throne as a child, and his reign was remembered for its cruelty. In 1699 he was murdered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kota-tinggi">Kota Tinggi</a> by the nobleman Megat Sri <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a>, whose pregnant wife he had had killed, and the bendahara then took the throne as Abdul Jalil IV.</p></div>
